> **Why this hotel?**  
> • It’s the most affordable of the three options while still offering a rooftop terrace and a free shuttle to the airport.  
> • The location is a short drive from the airport and close to several key attractions.

---

## 2️⃣ Attractions & Activities Near the Hotel

| Attraction | Distance | Type | Highlights |
|------------|----------|------|------------|
| **Parc des Buttes‑Chaumont** | 5.2 km | Park | Lush gardens, a lake, a grotto, and a suspension bridge. |
| **La Défense** | 8.1 km | Business District | Modern architecture, the Grande Arche, shopping, and a panoramic viewpoint. |
| **Museum of the History of France** | 12.4 km | Museum | Located in the Palais des Tuileries; offers a deep dive into French history. |
| **La Villette** | 14.3 km | Cultural Complex | Home to the Cité des Sciences, music venues, and seasonal festivals. |
| **Château de Fontainebleau** | 30.0 km | Historic Castle | UNESCO World Heritage site; a day‑trip worth the drive. |

> **Transport tips**  
> • **RER B** from **Aéroport Charles de Gaulle 2 – TGV** station (within the hotel) takes you to central Paris in ~30 min.  
> • A taxi or rideshare to the attractions takes 10–20 min, depending on traffic.

---

## 3️⃣ Suggested Sightseeing Routes

| Day | Route | Highlights | Approx. Time |
|-----|-------|------------|--------------|
| **Day 1 – Arrival & Relaxation** | Hotel → Parc des Buttes‑Chaumont → Dinner at a local bistro | Light walk, freshen up, enjoy a relaxed evening | 3–4 hrs |
| **Day 2 – Paris City Core** | Hotel → La Défense → Louvre → Tuileries → Eiffel Tower (optional river cruise) | Modern & classic Paris; iconic landmarks | 8–10 hrs |
| **Day 3 – Culture & Nature** | Hotel → La Villette → Musée d’Orsay → Seine River walk | Art, science, and scenic river views | 7–9 hrs |

> **Why these routes?**  
> • Each day starts and ends near your hotel, minimizing back‑and‑forth travel.  
> • The mix of parks, business districts, museums, and cultural complexes gives you a well‑rounded Paris experience.

